-- title:
--   Generic fibre of the j-finite chart is regular of dimension one
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian integral domain, $K_0$ a fraction field of $R$, and $F$ a field equipped with $R$- and $K_0$-algebra structures compatible in the sense that $R \to K_0 \to F$ is a tower. Let $j \in F$ be nonzero and transcendental over $R$, and assume that $F$ is finite-dimensional and separable over the intermediate field $K_0(j) =$ `IntermediateField.adjoin K₀ {j}`. Write $A_{\mathrm{fin}} =$ `chartAlgFin R F j` for the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of those elements of $F$ that are integral over the $R$-subalgebra $R[j]$ generated by $j$, that is, the integral closure of $R[j]$ in $F$. Then for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of the $K_0$-algebra $K_0 \otimes_R A_{\mathrm{fin}}$, the localisation of $K_0 \otimes_R A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ at $\mathfrak m$ is a regular local ring, and its Krull dimension, as an element of $\mathbb{N}_\infty$, equals $1$.
--
--   This is the statement that the generic fibre of the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model — the chart whose coordinate ring is the integral closure of $R[j]$ in $F$ — is regular of dimension one; after inverting the nonzero elements of $R$ one is looking at the integral closure of $K_0[j] \cong K_0[X]$ in the finite separable extension $F$, a Dedekind domain. It is used in the regularity statement for the stalks of the two-chart integral model at points of the generic fibre, and in the local analysis of the charts of $X_1$ at level-raising.
